{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778952017,"nonce":"qSG0qp7TXeoWOAB2m1VWxbGBwkk=","message":"Implemented graph projection slice on feature/ledger-graph-projection and fast-forwarded it into feature/ledger-program at c690582.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added src/ledger/graph-adapter.ts as the ledger-backed issue graph projection boundary.\n- Issue graph nodes now come from canonical ledger issues when ledger issue data exists, with repo/project aliases, labels, comments, conflict/outbox sync state, body excerpts, and layout metadata.\n- Ledger issue relationships now project as semantic graph edges. parent_child relationships become umbrella_child edges with hierarchical layout hints and label_default_visible=false.\n- In issue mode, auth requests and sessions are attached to issue nodes as evidence annotations/counts instead of standalone auth/session nodes. Active/idle/running sessions appear as live evidence; dead/ended sessions are counted historically but not emitted as live evidence.\n- Activity/work modes can resolve auth/session/work-unit issue edges through canonical ledger issue IDs, falling back to legacy metadata when needed.\n- Graph mode counts and repo/branch filters include ledger-backed issue/project data, which fixes the issue-mode count/layer mismatch when ledger data is the source of truth.\n- React Flow now respects layout rank/order hints for issue components, suppresses edge labels by default, and shows attached evidence in the right detail pane.\n\nVerification:\n- npm run build\n- npm test -- test/ledger-graph-adapter.test.ts test/graph.test.ts test/ledger-operational-links.test.ts\n- npm test (22 files, 296 tests)\n- Browser smoke on a seeded temp DB at http://127.0.0.1:19731/#/graph?mode=issue: two issue nodes rendered in parent/child columns, edge labels were absent by default, and evidence was visible in the detail pane.","files":null}]}